@startuml e2e_context_diagram
title "E2E Responsibility Layering (Events/Fields)"
skinparam stereotypePosition bottom

actor "Application" as APP

package "mw::com" as mw_com <<SEooC>> {

    component "Communication Management" as COMM_MGMT <<binding-independent>>

    component "E2E Manager" as E2E_MGR <<binding-independent>> {
        component "Protect (SkeletonEventBase)" as PROTECT
        component "Check (ProxyEventBase)" as CHECK
        component "State Machine" as SM <<Ticket 2>>
    }

    interface "Binding Interface Contract" as BINDING_IF

    component "LoLa Binding" as LOLA <<binding-specific>>
    component "SOME/IP Binding" as SOMEIP <<binding-specific, future>>
}

component "Transport" as TRANSPORT

APP -down-> COMM_MGMT
COMM_MGMT -down-> E2E_MGR
CHECK -right-> SM : RawE2ECheckResult\n(out of scope here, see SWP-279114)
E2E_MGR -down-> BINDING_IF
BINDING_IF -down-> LOLA
BINDING_IF -down-> SOMEIP
LOLA -down-> TRANSPORT
SOMEIP -down-> TRANSPORT

note right of E2E_MGR
  Binding-independent: owns E2EProtectContext (sender)
  and E2E check context (receiver). Binding is stateless
  w.r.t. E2E communication supervision.
end note

note right of BINDING_IF
  Binding only places/extracts precomputed header bytes
  at the transport-specific offset; it never computes
  E2E_PXXProtect()/E2E_PXXCheck() itself.
  ToDo: Need to align with revised e2e responsibility layering.
end note

@enduml
